      "worked": "Write each outcome as $(\\text{first spin},\\text{second spin})$. Pair each row label with each column label.\n\nFor first spin $1$: $(1,1),\\ (1,2),\\ (1,3)$.\n\nFor first spin $2$: $(2,1),\\ (2,2),\\ (2,3)$.\n\nFor first spin $3$: $(3,1),\\ (3,2),\\ (3,3)$.\n\nThere are $3\\times3=9$ possible outcomes.",
